.TH MM 1 "September 2026" "mm 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mm \- a runtime queue: add work, do the next thing, mark it done
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mm
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIarguments\fR]
.br
.B man mm
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mm
is a box you put items into at runtime.
Nothing appears unless you typed
.BR "mm add" .
There is no config file, no daily seed, and nothing repeats tomorrow
unless you add it again.
.PP
The ritual is:
.PP
.RS
.B mm add
.RI \*(lq task \*(rq
.br
.B mm
.br
.B mm done
.RE
.PP
Bare
.B mm
is the same as
.BR "mm next" .
.SH MODEL
Three containers, in precedence order:
.TP
.B interrupt stack
LIFO. Real urgency only
.RB ( "mm add \-p" ).
Preempts the queue, then unwinds like a call stack.
.TP
.B main queue
FIFO. Default work
.RB ( "mm add" ).
.TP
.B quick queue
Sub-1-minute trivia
.RB ( "mm add \-q" ).
Never auto-surfaced mid-task. Flush with
.BR "mm flush-quick" .
.PP
Blocked and suspended items are skipped. There are no gates.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Work
.TP
.B mm
.TQ
.B mm next
Show the active item and start its timer.
.TP
.B mm peek
Same glance, no timer.
.TP
.BI "mm done" " [id]"
Finish the active item (or that id) and advance.
.TP
.BI "mm add" " task"
Enqueue.
.B \-p
pushes an interrupt.
.B \-q
goes to the quick queue.
.TP
.BI "mm block" " [reason]"
Stuck: requeue and move on.
.TP
.BI "mm unblock " id " [\-\-front]"
Clear a block. Queue items can jump to the front.
.TP
.BI "mm suspend" " [id]"
Park without finishing.
.TP
.BI "mm resume" " [id]"
Bring one item back. Most recent if omitted.
.B \-\-all
restores every parked item.
.TP
.BI "mm move " id " queue|stack|quick [\-\-front]"
Reclassify, keep id and history.
.SS Housekeeping
.TP
.BI "mm rm " id
Remove an item.
.TP
.BI "mm edit " id " text"
Replace the item text.
.TP
.BI "mm note " id " text"
Append a note.
.TP
.BI "mm find " query
Search open items and the archive.
.TP
.B mm undo
Reverse the last mutation.
.TP
.B mm flush-quick
Clear the quick queue at a checkpoint.
.SS Look
.TP
.B mm status
Show all three containers.
.TP
.B mm stats
Today's counts. No cheerleading.
.TP
.B mm archive
.TQ
.B mm archive today
Finished items.
.TP
.B mm export
.RI [ json | md | csv ]
Dump open items and the archive.
.TP
.BI "mm log" " [n]"
Recent events (default 10).
.TP
.B mm help
Open this manual.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.mm/state.json
The only state file. Queue, stack, quick, archive, log, undo snapshots.
.TP
.I ~/.mm/state.json.lock
Exclusive lock while a command runs.
.PP
Override the directory with
.BR MM_HOME .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
.B 2
on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README.
